pkg:Evidence_v1_5_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.5.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: response to a direct user challenge asking whether the v1.4.0 'compliant' claim was actually comprehensively verified. Audited own tool usage first: only 2 of ~29 tools this framework now ships had ever been run against this register (backlog_pipeline_verify, backlog_validate). Ran a third, backlog_lineage_completeness_v1_1_0.py, for real. It requires backlog:LineageLayer individuals the shared TBox does not carry (they exist only in the framework's own internal register_abox) -- worked around locally by merging the public data rather than fabricating it, then ran the tool for real. Two outcomes: (1) a genuine, previously undetected defect in this register -- Epic/Story linkage only ever asserted the inverse partOf direction, never decomposesInto, which any SPARQL-based (non-OWL-inferencing) tool queries directly; reported 0 decomposition edges; fixed by adding the explicit decomposesInto triples; re-verified 4 edges now present, pipeline and L2 SHACL both re-confirmed clean after the fix. (2) The tool's LAYERS-table tier annotations do not reliably match current shape severities -- spot-checked MetricObservation specifically: the tool reports 'fails at L2', the actual shape (backlog_shacl_v1_72_0.ttl) enforces it at L4; this register's own clean L2 validate() run is consistent with the real shape, not the tool's stale annotation. Both findings filed as a proposal (00-proposals/Proposal_BRSF_LineageLayerGaps_v1_0_0.md) rather than fixed in the framework directly (B1/L-110). Checked and ruled not applicable to this register: backlog_number_origin and backlog_adoption_check only ever parse the framework's own TBox, never a register; backlog_reachability_gate checks class-design health of the vocabulary itself, not adopter content. The remaining 9 layers the completeness tool reports absent (MetricObservation, ExecutionTask, PlanningEvent, Iteration, Milestone, CrossCuttingInvariant, CostEstimate, Evidence, Forecast) are correctly and intentionally absent: this backlog has zero execution history by design (all items Proposed, per the user's own explicit instruction not to jump to implementation), and would become required as work actually begins, not now. Final state re-verified after every fix: pipeline order (5/5 digests reproduce), full SHACL at declared L2_EvidenceBound (0 sh:Violation, 86 sh:Warning)."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "60c59fdb6b4b196102679778c65a27768d54fd9738c2796d76d242333225fbc8"^^xsd:string .
